WEBVTT

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:20.560
Things unexpected, but not to be denied.

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:25.440
Join me now and take one step beyond

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:29.760
around the lives of all great men.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.320
History weaves romantic and colorful stories.

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:35.230
Many are based on facts.

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:38.130
And some are pure imagination.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:41.460
There are many wonderful stories told about the man.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:43.410
who for one terrible

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:44.960
and momentous winter.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:47.160
Occupy this house

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:49.970
But none is so.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:50.900
Little Noun

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.130
for awe-inspiring.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:54.310
as the events that took place here.

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:55.670
one evening.

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:57.690
Our very existence.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:00.660
well as our future.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:02.680
is largely dependent

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:04.590
on that remarkable

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:06.450
Night of decision.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:10.140
Sure, sure, Gypsy. We'll all die sooner or later.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:12.760
What about those supply wagons from Easton?

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:15.760
They're bringing good salt pork to fill our bellies.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:17.040
Thank you very much.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.150
Fresh clothes to put on our backs.

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:25.950
There will be no supply wagon.

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:27.140
That's it.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:29.040
I see only hunger.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:30.840
Suffering.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:33.220
I'm DEATH.

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:34.120
No way.

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:38.890
I see quite a bit of suffering for you, too, Gypsy.

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:40.790
We were told to stay out of camp.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:43.890
You and your rag-tailed friends with your tales of doom.

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:45.240
Be careful, boys.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:46.360
No!

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:48.510
They'll be coming at us through those trees.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:50.140
Take cover.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:50.820
Take cover!

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:53.280
Wow.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:56.400
That's all right.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:59.500
I'll be back before spring plant.

00:01:59.820 --> 00:01:59.980
What?

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:00.620
What will they do to them?

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:03.680
What?

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:09.040
Valley Forge, December 1777.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:13.690
The winter of despair is just beginning.

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:53.630
Thank you, sir.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:09.380
Do you know something else, Lieutenant?

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:10.890
I don't know.

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:11.720
Nox.

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:23.220
Whoa.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:26.860
Do they expect us to go on fighting without food and supplies?

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:29.700
That is precisely the point, Colonel.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:33.440
I believe those supply wagons were deliberately cancelled.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:35.140
Supplies are ample.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:38.960
but a large element in the Continental Congress would like us to give up.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.580
This is a form of persuasion.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:42.500
Wait.

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:47.310
part of this war, too.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:52.380
Congress has been contacted by agents of the British.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:55.900
with an offer that grants every one of our demands.

00:03:57.190 --> 00:03:58.310
Everything except independence.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:03:59.820
and is

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.660
Are the Congress ready to settle for that?

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:04.470
The good many gentlemen in the Congress are.

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:07.130
In the face of it, sir, why do you go on?

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:09.880
Are you ready to give up, Colonel?

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:26.550
What is that about?

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:29.970
It's another one of those gypsies, sir, fortune tellers.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:33.010
This one told some of the men that the supply wagons will never arrive.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:35.260
By whose order is he being flogged?

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:36.410
Make it warm.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:37.870
The order is countermanded.

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:38.820
Thank you.

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:49.270
Certainly you don't put any credence in that sort of thing, Danforth.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:51.730
Well, no, sir, but...

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:54.210
He could have learned about those wagons in a hundred different ways.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:57.540
General.

00:04:59.370 --> 00:04:59.950
This group.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:00.900
that wants to quit.

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:03.560
Just how important are they in Congress?

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:05.580
Very important.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:10.140
considerably in the minority, but...

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:12.880
They are making themselves felt.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:19.080
They even asked me for support.

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:19.990
you

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:22.110
But you were refused, of course.

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:24.350
Yes, yes, I refuse.

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:29.140
but I don't know that I had the right.

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:30.630
Sir?

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:33.950
12,000 men here in rags, colonel.

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:34.940
And starving.

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:38.480
Shouldn't they be consulted about any?

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:39.240
Settlement?

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:41.680
500 of them die every month.

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:43.120
of disease and privation.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:47.390
There is little glory or satisfaction in that kind of death.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:57.180
And then, of course,

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:00.520
are the dead.

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:08.520
I wonder how they would feel about our settling for anything less than they died for.

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:14.300
I don't know which side of the question you favor, sir.

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:18.070
Be honest, Colonel.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:22.920
this moment I do not know myself.

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:05.960
When will spring ever come?

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:15.410
I have the right

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:17.560
to decide the fate of so many.

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:57.840
God has come to your aid before. He will again. I am Otunka, chief of Shawnee. 22 summers have come and gone since we met.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.340
Battle of Monongahela.

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:02.800
Yes, of course.

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:10.920
July 1755, I was leading a detachment of Virginians under the command of General Braddock.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:18.710
Redcoats stood tall in sunlight like field of dry corn waiting for harvest night.

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:20.450
Yes, it was a slaughter.

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:25.530
We lost half the entire British colonial army that day.

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:28.650
All British officers in field fell.

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:29.900
Yes.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.000
or wounded, all but you, Washington.

00:08:35.590 --> 00:08:36.210
Remember well.

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:40.560
Otumkas fired at Washington again and again.

00:08:41.470 --> 00:08:43.150
Fifteen bullets at the heart.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:46.220
Not one found its mark.

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:51.240
Has caused Otumkas much wonder.

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:59.810
Very fortunate that our spirit...

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:04.280
He protected Washington that day for good and great purpose.

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:09.570
Wish I could believe it.

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:03.460
We're going back to our farms where we can be of some good to somebody.

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:05.880
You'll be shot down before you can get a hundred yards.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:09.340
Maybe, but it's better than slow starvation for a lost cause.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:14.360
We're going home, General.

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:18.220
We found out the gypsy was right about those supply wagons, too.

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:19.340
We're going home.

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:21.140
I go.

00:10:22.340 --> 00:10:22.560
Go.

00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:26.400
If we have sunk to the level of animals, turning one upon another,

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:29.230
then perhaps our cause is already lost.

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:33.220
They're coming through the trees!

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:34.200
Hold it!

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:44.920
Pa, I meant to get to the chickens sooner, only

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:48.600
Jason hurt his knee up by the crick in the south pasture.

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:50.200
I'll get to it sooner tomorrow.

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:13.910
never consider myself a mystique mon general but i can find no ready explanation for what impressed

00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:20.250
that indian so profoundly what they said about that battle was all the truth was it not oh my

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:26.150
dear lafayette he must have been just a creation in my own troubled mind he must have been there

00:11:27.100 --> 00:11:28.360
were no footprints in the snow

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.940
Tom Castle is supposed to have died in his own village two years ago.

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:33.880
What if he did?

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:36.130
What if he did?

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:42.890
That bullet hole in your cloak would be proof of his belief in your invulnerability.

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:44.200
His belief?

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:49.710
A man dead two years, talking nonsense,

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:54.820
an hallucination caused by remembering an impressive day in my youth.

00:11:55.350 --> 00:11:57.330
How many battles have you been in, Mon General?

00:11:58.440 --> 00:11:59.500
Scores, perhaps hundreds.

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:03.400
How many times have you been wounded?

00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:05.760
Never.

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:09.410
This has been a day of madness.

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:14.600
First me, then you, the gypsies' predictions,

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:17.330
a visit from a dead Indian.

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:29.980
Yet, and yet, I can remember very well the words I wrote in...

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.760
a letter to my brother after that battle.

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:32.850
I said,

00:12:35.050 --> 00:12:37.750
by the all-powerful dispensations of Providence.

00:12:39.650 --> 00:12:43.950
I have been protected beyond all human possibility and expectation.

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:44.440
Thank you very much.

00:12:44.870 --> 00:12:46.430
beyond all human

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:47.650
Possibility.

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:50.460
I agree.

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:52.980
My dear Lafayette.

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:55.440
You are an incurable romantic.

00:12:57.580 --> 00:12:58.220
Mon Général.

00:12:58.860 --> 00:12:59.980
I am a Frenchman.

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:05.640
