00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:23.100
projects to keep them busy.

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:26.940
achieve the highest level of preparation for our spring campaign.

00:20:27.900 --> 00:20:28.600
Spring campaign.

00:20:29.300 --> 00:20:29.980
But I thought...

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:30.900
You thought what, Major?

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:32.090
Weld.

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:34.440
I assumed that your plans were...

00:20:35.020 --> 00:20:35.520
That is.

00:20:36.140 --> 00:20:37.720
I assumed that your mood was...

00:20:37.720 --> 00:20:38.360
Pardon me, sir.

00:20:39.140 --> 00:20:40.780
But we are despairing of the future.

00:20:41.450 --> 00:20:42.310
If you know something,

00:20:43.180 --> 00:20:46.140
If you are free to tell us the basis of this sudden optimism.

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:48.500
Some news about the French, perhaps.

00:20:49.770 --> 00:20:51.170
News of a victory in the North.

00:20:51.850 --> 00:20:52.750
There is no news coming.

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:54.120
Good or bad.

00:20:55.620 --> 00:20:56.680
We must make our own good news.

00:20:58.020 --> 00:20:58.900
But I can say...

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.080
I am now confident.

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:03.560
that this war will end in our favor.

00:21:04.760 --> 00:21:06.220
and with complete victory.

00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:07.260
Victory!

00:21:08.060 --> 00:21:08.960
But surely, General,

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:10.490
The meeting is adjourned, gentlemen.

